    {
      "id": "process",
      "hidden": false,
      "layout": "auto",
      "background": null,
      "header": "",
      "aside": "",
      "speaker": "Cleaning and organizing affect the result as much as any other step. The book follows this whole process, not just the estimation step.",
      "print": "Source: gabors-data-analysis.com/whythisbook",
      "steps": 0,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "title",
          "content": "Data analysis is a process",
          "step": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "list",
          "ordered": true,
          "size": "normal",
          "items": [
            {
              "content": "Start with a question",
              "number": 1
            },
            {
              "content": "Collect data, or check if existing data can answer it",
              "number": 2
            },
            {
              "content": "Clean and organize the data",
              "number": 3
            },
            {
              "content": "Explore it to learn the context",
              "number": 4
            },
            {
              "content": "Pick a method, run it, check robustness",
              "number": 5
            },
            {
              "content": "Interpret, visualize, and answer the question",
              "number": 6
            }
          ],
          "step": 0,
          "start": 1,
          "progressive": false
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "gap",
      "hidden": false,
      "layout": "statement",
      "background": null,
      "header": "",
      "aside": "",
      "speaker": "This is the main reason the book exists. The rest of the deck shows how it does it.",
      "print": "",
      "steps": 0,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "title",
          "content": "Methods textbooks rarely teach the project",
          "step": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "size": "normal",
          "content": "Econometrics and data science textbooks are often excellent at teaching methods. But they say little about how to carry out an actual analysis from beginning to end.",
          "step": 0
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "size": "normal",
          "content": "Students learn that from projects, advisors and peers. We wanted a textbook that teaches it, too.",
          "step": 0
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "structure",
      "hidden": false,
      "layout": "data",
      "background": null,
      "header": "",
      "aside": "",
      "speaker": "We selected the most widely used methods that tend to work well, so each one gets a detailed treatment and we can compare them, in general and in the case studies.",
      "print": "Source: gabors-data-analysis.com (home page, chapters page)",
      "steps": 0,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "title",
          "content": "Four parts, 24 chapters",
          "step": 0
        },
